      "chb_s5_title": "Chassis and Boom FAQ",
      "chb_f1_q": "Do you weld high-strength steels such as S690QL and S960QL?",
      "chb_f1_a": "Yes. We hold WPQRs qualified to EN ISO 15614-1 for S690QL, S960QL, Strenx 700/960 and S700MC. Preheat follows EN 1011-2, H5-class consumables are used and interpass temperature is recorded for every weld.",
      "chb_f2_q": "What does the 35 m submerged arc line bring to chassis fabrication?",
      "chb_f2_a": "Longitudinal beams and box sections are welded in one setup with constant parameters. Fewer start-stop points, a homogeneous seam and better straightness over long lengths, with no repositioning time.",
      "chb_f3_q": "Can you deliver the chassis module painted and ready for assembly?",
      "chb_f3_a": "Yes. Cutting, bending, welding, machining, blasting and painting are planned under one contract; operations done at partner facilities pass ArmaWeld's incoming inspection. The module is delivered to go straight into your assembly line.",
      "chb_f4_q": "Can you produce a chassis without existing drawings?",
      "chb_f4_a": "Yes. We measure your existing part and prepare the shop drawing and WPS; parts to be revised are redesigned by reverse engineering. Production starts after you approve the drawing.",
      "chb_f5_q": "Do you supply chassis and booms to manufacturers in Europe?",
      "chb_f5_a": "Yes. We produce for machine and equipment builders in Europe under EN 1090 and EN ISO 3834-2, with an English document file. EXW or DAP delivery options are offered in the quote and order status is tracked live in the customer portal.",
