      "px_hz_22": "MIG/MAG and TIG fabrication with approved WPS in carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminium and high-strength steels.",
      "px_hz_23": "Project-Based Flexibility",
      "px_hz_24": "We plan production from single prototypes to medium-volume series. There is no minimum order.",
      "px_hz_25": "Optimised Cost & Transparent Quotes",
      "px_hz_26": "Engineering discipline raises operational efficiency; unnecessary costs are removed and you receive a transparent, competitive quote.",
      "px_hz_27": "Fully Integrated Process",
      "px_hz_28": "Welding, NDT and painting in-house; sheet cutting and bending are coordinated within the project plan. One point of contact and traceable delivery.",
      "px_hz_29": "Engineer Supervision",
      "px_hz_30": "Every contract project gets a quality plan under an IWE/IWT certified engineer, and welding parameters are recorded.",
      "px_hz_31": "Production Process: From Drawing to Delivery",
      "px_hz_32": "Technical Review & Quote",
      "px_hz_33": "We review the drawing or sample, define material group, welding process (MIG/MAG or TIG), tolerances and documentation, then prepare the quote.",
      "px_hz_34": "WPS Selection & Production Plan",
      "px_hz_35": "An approved welding procedure (WPS/WPQR) is selected and a production plan with welding sequence and inspection points is drawn up.",
      "px_hz_36": "Welding & NDT",
      "px_hz_37": "Qualified welders carry out MIG/MAG or TIG welding, and the required NDT (UT, MT, PT, VT) is applied.",
      "px_hz_38": "After dimensional checks, visual inspection and quality records are complete, parts ship with the manufacturing documentation.",
      "px_hz_39": "Which Welding Process Suits Your Project?",
